# React layers

Keep the same roles inside `packages/react/src/<domain>/` (and subdomains like `wizard/upload/`, `share-viewer/`).

## Folder contract

Every domain (and subdomain) is **only** these directories. No loose files beside them (`types.ts`, `actions.ts`, `constants.ts` at the folder root).

| Dir | Holds | Imports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `feature/` | Owns hooks; composes layout; passes props into `ui/` | `hooks/`, `ui/`, `util/`, `@repo/react/design-system` |
| `ui/` | Presentational leaves — props in, elements out | other `ui/`, `util/` types, `@repo/react/design-system` |
| `hooks/` | React state, wiring, subscriptions | `util/`, `data-access/` |
| `util/` | Pure work, **types**, **action creators**, view-model helpers | `@repo/shared`, other util |
| `data-access/` | GraphQL documents + generated types | — |
| `constants/` | Frozen tables / defaults (when they are not a single util module) | `util/` types |
| `icons/` | Tiny SVG components | — |

`README.md` may sit at the domain root. Public re-exports live in a domain-root `index.ts` that the package export map points at — not a stray `index.ts` inside `feature/`.

```
packages/react/src/design-system/file-explorer/
  feature/
  ui/
  hooks/
  util/
```

`apps/web` routes compose only: pass ids, callbacks, and public `@repo/react/...` features.

## Compose edge

```tsx
import { ItemList, Panel } from '@repo/react/design-system';

import { useItems } from '../hooks/use-items';

export function ItemsPanel({ collectionId }: ItemsPanelProps) {
  const { items, dispatch } = useItems({ collectionId });

  return (
    <Panel>
      <ItemList dispatch={dispatch}>
        <ItemList.Toolbar />
        {items.map((item) => (
          <ItemList.Row key={item.id} item={item} />
        ))}
      </ItemList>
    </Panel>
  );
}
```

Hooks at the top → map the view model → nested UI. Domain work stays in `hooks/` + `util/` (`react-feature-hooks.mdc`, `pure-domain.mdc`).

## Presentational leaf

Content control comes from the design system (`Input`, `Pin`, `Button`, `Text`). Layout around it is `Stack` / `Group` / `Panel` (`design-system-layout.mdc`):

```tsx
import { Pin, Stack, Text } from '@repo/react/design-system';
import { SpaceConfig } from '@repo/shared';

export function PinBlock({ value, onChange, error }: PinBlockProps) {
  return (
    <Stack gap="tight">
      <Text variant="label">PIN</Text>
      <Pin
        length={SpaceConfig.SHARE_PIN_LENGTH}
        value={value}
        onChange={onChange}
        error={error}
        mask
        ariaLabel="Share PIN"
      />
    </Stack>
  );
}
```

## Keeping layers healthy

- Data wiring and mutations live in `hooks/` / `feature/`; `ui/` stays presentational.
- Merge / validate / update logic lives in `util/` once a `feature/` or hook would grow past a thin compose (`tiny-files.mdc`).
- Shared helpers used by several subdomains live in the **parent** domain `util/` / `hooks/` (`imports-and-files.mdc`).
- Layout and controls come from `@repo/react/design-system`. `@mantine/core` stays inside DS primitive files (`design-system-layout.mdc`).
